				\begin{document} $$ \text{accuracy} = \frac{\text{TP}+\text{TN}}{n^{+} + n^{-}} = \frac{\text{TP}+\text{TN}}{\text{TP}+\text{TN}+\text{FP}+\text{FN}}   $$ \end{document}accuracy=TP+TNn++n−=TP+TNTP+TN+FP+FN

By definition, the accuracy is defined for every confusion matrix M and ranges in the real unit interval [0,1]; the best value 1.00 corresponds to perfect classification \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
